Git bisect: Git bisect is a debugging tool that helps to find a commit that introduced bug using binary search through the commit history
•	Commands:
•	Start: git bisect start
•	Mark current commit as bad: git bisect bad
•	Mark a known good commit: git bisect good <commit-id>
•	If bug exists: git bisect bad
•	If bug does not exist: git bisect good
•	Finish: git bisect reset: returns to original branch
